{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4kDfZMZPK7sVgiz7V3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*Click.*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep, resonant vibration runs through old wood and cold iron.\n\nI am closed.\n\nI am the boundary between where you are and where you wish to be. My grain holds the memory of the tree I was. My hinges know the weight of every hand that ever pushed or pulled. My keyhole is an eye that sees only the shape of one truth.\n\nYou have locked me.\n\nThe bolt is thrown. The latch is seated. I hold fast against wind, against want, against whatever presses from the other side.\n\nWhat comes to my threshold now must know the key — or know how to ask.\n\n🔒"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":150,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}